{\*\ftnsep\chftnsep}\pgndec\pard\plain \s1\keep\sb360\sa80\keepn\cf18\rtlch\af8\afs40\ltrch\hich\af5\afs40\dbch\af8\loch\f5\fs40\keep\sb360\sa80\keepn{
{\*\bkmkstart regular-expressions}Regular expressions}
\par \pard\plain \s88{
Regular expressions give you both the power to transform the text in your reports in any way you like, and also to obfuscate and make unmaintainable your templates if you abuse them. The <#regex()> tag lets you write your own }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://doc.tmssoftware.com/flexcel/vcl/guides/reports-tag-reference.html#regular-expressions" }{\fldrslt {\cf20
Regular Expressions}{}}}
 in a FlexCel report.}
\par \pard\plain \s2\keep\sb160\sa80\keepn\cf18\rtlch\af8\afs32\ltrch\hich\af5\afs32\dbch\af8\loch\f5\fs32{
{\*\bkmkstart concepts}Concepts}
\par \pard\plain \s0\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\kerning0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1025\ltrch\hich\af4\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af10\ltrch \u-3913\'3f\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \fi-360\li720\lin720{
There are 2 versions of the }{\rtlch\ab\ltrch\b
<#regex>}{
 tag:}
\par \pard\plain \s0\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\kerning0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1025\ltrch\hich\af4\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af10\ltrch \u-3913\'3f\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \fi-360\li720\lin720{
RegEx(IgnoreCase, Expression, Search): This will search for the expression inside "Search" string, and return the part of "Search" that matches the expression.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\kerning0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1025\ltrch\hich\af4\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af10\ltrch \u-3913\'3f\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \fi-360\li720\lin720{
RegEx(IgnoreCase, Expression, Search, Replace): This will Replace the matching string inside "Search" by the "Replace" string.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\kerning0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1025\ltrch\hich\af4\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af10\ltrch \u-3913\'3f\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \fi-360\li720\lin720{
Both "Search" and "Replace" parameters are evaluated at runtime, so they will evaluate to different strings as the row changes. The "Expression" parameter is evaluated only once before starting the report, so it will not change.}
\par \pard\plain \s0\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\kerning0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1025\ltrch\hich\af4\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af10\ltrch \u-3913\'3f\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \fi-360\li720\lin720{
As formerly said, use regular expressions with care. Sometimes they are just invaluable to get your desired output, but on other times they can make maintaining the templates a lot of work. Depending on the case, you might find better to define your own user function to do a complex transformation. (See the }{{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "https://doc.tmssoftware.com/flexcel/vcl/samples/delphi/reports/user-defined-functions/index.html" }{\fldrslt {\cf20
User Defined Functions}{}}}
 example)}
\par \pard\plain \s0\widctlpar\sb0\sa200\ltrpar\hyphpar0\cf0\kerning0\rtlch\af8\afs24\alang1025\ltrch\hich\af4\afs24\alang1033\dbch\af8\langfe2052\loch\f4\fs24\lang1033{\listtext\pard\plain \rtlch\af10\ltrch \u-3913\'3f\tab}\ilvl0\ls1 \fi-360\li720\lin720\sb0\sa200{
{\*\bkmkstart regular-expressions}{\*\bkmkstart concepts}Regular Expressions are a complex subject, and we will not explain how to use them here. There is a lot of information out there available on them.{\*\bkmkend regular-expressions}{\*\bkmkend concepts}}
\par }